WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.635
-You know my next guest
as Peter Kavinsky

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.337
from the "To All the Boys"
franchise.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.074
He has been called
the Internet's boyfriend.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.642
So -- And everyone's
freaking out

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.344
that he's on the show tonight.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.945
The third and final film
of the series,

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.614
"To All the Boys:
Always and Forever,"

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.949
begins streaming
on Netflix next Friday.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.018
Here is Noah Centineo.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:23.389
Noah, man, you are a good actor.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.490
-Oh.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.893
-You faked out
me and Dolly Parton.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.695
-Have you you heard the truth?

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:30.996
-No.

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:32.498
The truth is pretty good.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.433
-What's the truth?

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:38.571
-The truth is, I brought my cat
to a friend's house

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.206
but had to send him home
in a taxi

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.975
because he didn't get along
with my friend's dog.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.143
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.379
Wait, the cat by himself?

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.549
[ Laughs ]

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.251
Did he make it?
Did he make it home?

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.252
-He made it!

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.853
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.790
That is really funny, dude.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.958
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.760
I'd love that
you trust the cab that much.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.830
Like, "Just make sure this cat
gets to its home."

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.165
-But you know
what I thought about?

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.532
I thought about -- I was like --

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.435
I gave him -- Like, I tipped him
pretty heavy, you know?

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.371
I was like, "Hey, man,
he's an outdoor cat.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.906
Just get it to the address,
open the door.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.641
He'll know what to do."

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.844
He could have just driven,
like, two blocks

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.446
and then let the cat out,
and he didn't.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.647
-That is genius.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.683
That is a great --
That's a great story.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.984
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.285
Well, last time
you were on the show,

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:30.123
you were here in studio,
and then everything shut down.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.557
I haven't been able
to talk to you.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.359
What have you been doing
with all your time at home?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.094
Have you learned anything new,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.228
picked up any new hobbies?

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.297
Nothing.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.165
-You know,
it started off with, like,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.733
staying up -- For some reason
in the beginning,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.435
of, like,
the first lockdown in L.A.,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:46.338
I stayed awake until 6:30
in the morning every single day

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:49.342
and listened to, like, lo-fi
and, like, cried

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:53.646
and, like [Laughs] just, like,
wrote a lot of different things.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.248
-Yeah.
-It was really interesting.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.349
And then I started --
I started doing this

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:58.518
because of my buddy,
Tom McCarthy.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.321
I started doing
this thing called Wim Hof.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.389
And it's, like,
diaphragmatic breathing.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.324
Have you heard of it?
-No. Honestly, yeah.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:07.660
I actually almost passed out
trying it.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.762
-[ Laughs ]
-I'm serious.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.063
Is that the thing --
-Yeah, no.

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.532
I have passed out doing it.
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:17.103
-But, like, part of it's
cold exposure.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.606
-Oh.
-And so, like, I started taking,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.808
like, really cold showers
every single day.

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.211
-Yeah, I tried that.
-And it was like --

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.745
It was a whole --

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:30.316
It was a whole -- I don't know.
It was like a new world.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.951
-But you took it
to a new level, though,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.553
because we have a photo here.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.921
It's you --
'Cause I was wondering,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.656
you're in a garbage can
full of ice.

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:39.292
And I was like,
"Well, that's it.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.528
He's officially cracked."
[ Laughs ]

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.095
It's like, "He's gone."
-"Goodbye, Noah.

00:02:43.095 --> 00:02:44.897
He's gone."
[ Laughs ]

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.833
-I'm just gonna move
to the Swiss Alps.

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.335
-Dude, I mean, lookit.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.004
What is going on there?
Talk to me.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:56.742
-So -- So -- So I moved
to Florida last summer for --

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.544
I was gonna go just for
my birthday to see my dad,

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.679
'cause he lives in Florida
and some friends.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.414
And I ended up staying there
for about three months.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.884
And I was still doing
the Wim Hof daily.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.086
It was like a daily practice.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.021
But I got sick and tired
of cold showers,

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.622
and so I went to Lowe's,
and I bought

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:12.692
a 96-gallon trash bin

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.728
and would fill it halfway with
ice and the rest with water.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:19.399
So that was my cold exposure
every single day,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.000
like 15 minutes.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.269
-I want to talk
about your new movie.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:26.105
This is the third, and this is
the final of the series,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.341
the final installment
of "To All the Boys."

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:32.011
I mean, can you believe you
and Lana through --

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.613
This is --
You'll never forget each other.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.614
I mean, this is, like,
a major part of your life.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.683
I mean, for the rest, right?
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.251
-I mean...
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.319
It was like we went --

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.622
It's been almost four years...

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.757
-Yeah.
-...you know, just her and I.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.892
-And also just becoming famous
and all this stuff.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.495
But the chemistry is phenomenal
with you guys.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.896
Obviously, everyone
always brings it up.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:54.566
But I heard there was a story
that you actually met --

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:56.936
Before you got the parts,

00:03:56.936 --> 00:04:00.506
you met,
and there was not chemistry.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.141
-Well -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.809
-Did you hear this?
-It was --

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.178
It was -- So, okay.

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:10.149
So, you audition
for a role, right?

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.450
You go into a room

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.319
with strangers,
casting directors.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.355
You don't know them, and you're
auditioning for the role.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:18.424
And so what I like to do
with my auditions is,

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.728
I low-key like to, like,
run lines

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.230
before the actual chemistry
and before the actual audition

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.765
with other people in the room,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.967
because I feel like
it's a good way to break the ice

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.136
with, like,
reading with a stranger.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.605
So I see Lana
at the chemistry read,

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.374
and I-I thought that --

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.608
I didn't realize
that she had booked the role.

00:04:36.608 --> 00:04:39.678
I thought she was also
there chemistry reading

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.949
as one of three girls
like I was one of four guys.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.651
And so I'm like, "Hey,
do you want to --

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:45.818
Would you maybe
want to run lines?"

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.553
And she's like, "No, I'm okay."

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.890
Like, in her head, she's like,
"I got this. I'm good."

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.292
-Yeah, what are you doing? Like,
"No, I got the part, dude.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.694
You're the one
who's auditioning, buddy."

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:57.096
-[ Laughs ]
-"I already got the part."

00:04:57.096 --> 00:05:00.632
Wow. That is so not smooth.
I love it.

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:02.068
-I forgot about it.
She brought it up to me.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.169
She was like,
"Do you remember this?"

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.537
And I'm like, "No, I don't."

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:08.107
-Wow. And look at you guys now.
It's awesome, buddy.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:11.443
Congrats on this,
and what a fun trilogy.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:12.645
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.613
Here's Noah Centineo
and Lana Condor

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:17.150
in "To All the Boys:
Always and Forever."

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.018
Take a look.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.988
-Agent Covey.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.022
-What's happening?
-Don't look at me.

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:26.959
Your mission,
should you choose to accept it,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.530
is to meet me back here
in the lobby at 2100 hours.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.731
We're going out.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.166
-Where are we going?
-Don't look at me.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.702
That information's classified.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.038
-I'm pretty sure we're
supposed to stay in our rooms.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.073
-Intel suggests
that the chaperones

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:44.176
are going to be at the hotel bar
getting absolutely wasted,

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:45.611
giving us a clear exit.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.346
Do you accept the mission?

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:48.981
-I do.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.517
-Very good.
I'll see you at 2100 hours.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.720
♪♪

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.255
-Noah Centineo, everybody.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.524
"To All the Boys:
Always and Forever,"

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.694
will be streaming on Netflix
starting next Friday.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:04.697
Hey, say hi to your cat for me,
okay, bud?

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.199
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

